# =============================================================================
# HRRP Pipeline — .gitignore
#
# This repo is intended to END UP PUBLIC, and it will hold real Snowflake
# credentials in .env during development. Everything is excluded BEFORE the
# first commit: `git rm` later removes the file but leaves every prior version
# in the object store. One forgotten line is permanent.
#
# WHY DENY-BY-DEFAULT: `/*` ignores everything at the root, and the things that
# belong in the repo are added back by name below. A new file at the root is
# therefore ignored the moment it exists, with nothing to remember. Adding
# something is the deliberate act; excluding it is the default.
#
# NOTE: `/*` is anchored to the root level only. It does not reach nested paths
# like src/ingestion/__pycache__/, so those need their own rules further down.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Deny everything at the root -------------------------------------------
/*

# ---- Then allow back, explicitly -------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/.env.example
!/main.py
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt
!/hrrp_pipeline_blueprint.md
!/src/
!/scripts/
!/sql/
!/tests/
!/docs/
!/dbt_project/

# ---- Belt and braces: the sensitive ones, named ----------------------------
# Redundant calls with `/*` above and kept deliberately. It makes the intent legible
# to a human scanning this file, and it survives someone later "tidying up" the
# `/*` line without understanding what it was doing.
#
#   .env                 live Snowflake credentials
#   data/                ~169 MB of CMS CSVs. HCAHPS alone is 101 MB, over
#                        GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. Freely re-downloadable.
#   HRRP_BUILD_BRIEF.md  strategy document housing no design.
#   ROADMAP.md           working build checklist, not a published document. A
#                        list of unchecked boxes reads as incomplete work, and
#                        once the build is done it is redundant with the code.
#                        Forward-looking direction belongs in the README.

.env
*.pem
*.p8
credentials.json
data/
HRRP_BUILD_BRIEF.md
ROADMAP.md
.venv/
venv/
.claude/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store

# ---- Nested paths: NOT covered by `/*` -------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/

# ---- Power BI --------------------------------------------------------------
# The published dashboard file IS a deliverable — reviewers should be able to
# download and open it. Under deny-by-default it needs an explicit allow when
# it exists, e.g.:
#     !/docs/hrrp_dashboard.pbix
# Before committing one, check it: an Import-mode .pbix embeds the data and the
# Snowflake account identifier.

# dbt writes a per-user anonymous id here.
.user.yml
